nfs-ganesha (15.10-1+ezgh2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * d/p/0001-tls-fail-startup-on-a-bad-certificate-and-reload-it-on-SIGHUP.patch:
    ganesha.nfsd exits at startup when TLS_CONFIG enables TLS and its
    certificate or key fails to load; SIGHUP rereads TLS_CONFIG and swaps a
    freshly loaded certificate in for new connections (established sessions
    keep theirs; a failed load keeps the current one).
  * nfs-ganesha-ceph and nfs-ganesha-rados-grace depend on libcephfs2 and
    librados2 at exactly 20.2.4-1noble: libcephfs2 needs libceph-common's
    private symbols from the same librados2 build.
  * nfs-ganesha depends on libtirpc-common: ntirpc reads /etc/netconfig and
    ganesha.nfsd exits at startup without it.

